The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (nft_set_elem_active(&rbe->ext, genmask)) {
    ...
    *ext = &rbe->ext;
    return -EEXIST;
}
```
Reason:
The condition checks if the existing element is active, and if so, it returns `-EEXIST` without properly handling the case where an inactive element is being re-added. This leads to the failure of selecting the next branch to inspect, causing an infinite loop.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
else if (nft_set_elem_active(&rbe->ext, genmask)) {
    *ext = &rbe->ext;
    return -EEXIST;
} else {
    p = &parent->rb_left;
}
```
Reason:
The patch restricts the check for active elements to the `EEXIST` case only, ensuring that when an inactive element is re-added, the logic can progress to the next branch in the tree instead of looping endlessly. This allows the insertion logic to function correctly without getting stuck.

